{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 36, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.1-8b-instruct", "content": "the social network is a 2010 american biographical drama film directed by david fincher and written by Aaron sorkin. the film is based on the book \"the accidental billionaire\" by ben mezrich and tells the story of the founding of the social networking site facebook and the subsequent lawsuits that followed.\n\nthe film stars jesse eisenberg as mark zuckerberg, the co-founder and ceo of facebook, and justin timberlake as sean parker, the co-founder and initial president of the site. the supporting cast includes andrew garfield as eduardo saverin, the russian immigrant and college friend who helped finance facebook, and armie hammer as cambridge university student andrew mccollum, who was one of the first people to create a social networking site.\n\nthe film begins with the story of mark zuckerberg's high school days, where he creates a website called \"facemash\" that becomes a huge success. zuckerberg is then approached by his college friends, sean parker and eduardo saverin, to help them create a social networking site for harvard students. the site, called \"facebook,\" quickly gains popularity and spreads to other colleges and universities across the united states.\n\nas the film progresses, we see the rise of facebook and the subsequent lawsuits that followed. sean parker, who was initially the president of facebook, is portrayed as a charismatic and ambitious individual who is driven by his desire to succeed. mark zuckerberg, on the other hand, is portrayed as a brilliant but awkward and introverted individual who is often at odds with his co-founders.\n\nthe film also explores the themes of friendship, ambition, and the consequences of success. it raises questions about the ethics of facebook's early days, including the site's use of user data and its impact on users' personal relationships.\n\nthe film features a talented ensemble cast, with outstanding performances from jesse eisenberg and justin timberlake. eisenberg's portrayal of mark zuckerberg is particularly noteworthy, as he brings a depth and nuance to the character that is both captivating and heartbreaking.\n\nthe film's direction by david fincher is also noteworthy, as he brings a sense of style and sophistication to the film. the cinematography is sleek and modern, capturing the fast-paced and often chaotic world of the facebook founders.\n\nthe film's score by trent reznor and atticus ross is also a highlight, as they create a haunting and atmospheric soundtrack that perfectly captures the mood and tone of the film.\n\noverall, \"the social network\" is a gripping and thought-provoking film that raises important questions about the impact of technology on our lives. it is a must-see for anyone interested in the story of facebook and its founders, and it is a testament to the power of storytelling and the importance of exploring the complexities of human nature.\n\nrating: 9.5/10", "logprobs": [{"token": "the", "logprob": -0.045232724}, {"token": " social", "logprob": -0.0016868184}, {"token": " network", "logprob": -7.6293654e-06}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -0.18040486}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.00012385078}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -0.32515162}, {"token": "201", "logprob": -2.9086643e-05}, {"token": "0", "logprob": -3.933899e-06}, {"token": " american", "logprob": -0.3342006}, {"token": " bi", "logprob": -0.0031711787}, {"token": "ographical", "logprob": -0.00043990472}, {"token": " drama", "logprob": -0.011117537}, {"token": " film", "logprob": -0.00057299406}, {"token": " directed", "logprob": -0.18416922}, {"token": " by", "logprob": -0.0021900972}, {"token": " david", "logprob": -0.009290322}, {"token": " fin", "logprob": -0.00041380903}, {"token": "cher", "logprob": -2.682173e-05}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -0.2561861}, {"token": " written", "logprob": -0.0026351034}, {"token": " by", "logprob": -3.3378547e-06}, {"token"